8822154" ext-link-type="pubmed"/><abstract><p>Correction to McPoil TG, Cornwall MW, Medoff L, Vicenzion B, Fosberg K, Hilz D. Arch height change during sit-to-stand: an alternative for the navicular drop test. Journal of Foot and Ankle Research 2008; 1:3.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><sec><title>Correction</title><p>Correction to be made on the spelling of an author's name and email address in the publication of this work [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>], as the mistake was not caught prior to publication. The name to be corrected is Kelly K. Fosberg and the correct corresponding email address is <email>kellykaydpt@yahoo.com</email>.</p></sec></body><back><ref-list><ref id="B1"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>McPoil</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><name><surname>Cornwall</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Medoff</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Vicenzion</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Fosberg</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilz</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><article-title>Arch height change during sit-to-stand: an alternative for the navicular drop test</article-title><source>J Foot Ankle Res</source><year>2008</year><volume>1</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>3</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1757-1146-1-3</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18822154</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>